## Rules
- English for code, comments, logs, docs, commits and PRs. Player-facing text through i18n (en + fr).
- Branch `<type>/<issue>-<slug>`; Conventional Commits; one PR per issue with `Closes #n`;
  PR body: What / Why / How it was tested / Risk & revert.
- Open your PR yourself once `make check` passes and the end-of-task review is clean. Merge,
  tag, release or deploy only inside a chantier the maintainer approved on the review stack
  (the orchestrator runs the chantier merge plan); never push to the default branch, delete
  branches or touch secrets. Workflow: agent-kit `docs/WORKFLOW.md`.
- Live project state (chantiers, decisions, next steps) is in the private ops repo
  `Arffornia/ops` `STATE.md`; read it at the start of a session (`resume` skill) when you can.
- Do not replace the owner's libraries (Nexus_*, launcher modules) with third-party ones: improve them.
- `needs-decision` issues and design choices belong to the maintainer: ask, do not choose.
- Unfixed security weaknesses: neutral wording in public issues and PRs, no exploit details.
- Finish with evidence (command + result), not claims. Update `PROGRESS.md` before you stop
  when work is unfinished.
- **Review before handing back**: a non-trivial change gets `/arffornia:review` (fresh finder and
  verifier subagents, confirmed findings only). The Stop hook asks once per tree; there is no AI
  review in CI.
- **Improve the harness**: when the user corrects how you work, a guard or hook fires again and
  again, a skill misfires, or you hit friction or find a better way, record it with
  `/arffornia:harness-feedback` (issue in Arffornia/agent-kit, evidence + proposed patch).
- **Learning cards**: when you do or find something genuinely state of the art that the
  maintainer would want to learn, draft a card with `/arffornia:learning-card`.
- **Reporting**: every PR, issue, commit, artifact or page you mention to a human is a full
  clickable URL (`https://github.com/Arffornia/<repo>/pull/<n>`) with a one-line summary,
  grouped and ordered by what the human should do (review/merge, decide, FYI). Never
  "I opened the PR" without the link.
- Mechanical rules every change follows: `GOLDEN_PRINCIPLES.md`.

## Where knowledge lives
| Need | Look in |
|---|---|
| Conventions for the files you are editing | `.claude/rules/*.md` (loaded automatically by path) |
| How to review, what is risky | `REVIEW.md`, `risk.yml` (read by `/arffornia:review`) |
| Why something is the way it is | `docs/adr/` |
| Quality per area and known gaps | `QUALITY_SCORE.md` |
| Workflows (ticket → PR, publish, tests) | `/arffornia:<skill>` from the agent-kit plugin |
| Current work and next step | `PROGRESS.md`, `docs/exec-plans/active/` |

